We propose a Gaussian Process $(\mathcal{GP})$ model to approximate the unknown function $\upvarpi$.
%A $\mathcal{GP}$ is a probabilistic non-parametric approach of modelling complex functions from observed data. A $\mathcal{GP}$ is formally defined as a collection of random variables, any finite number of which follows a joint Gaussian distribution \cite{Rasmussen_Williams2006}. Unlike deterministic models that provide a single "best fit" to the data, the $\mathcal{GP}$  provides a distribution over functions, making it particularly attractive for applications requiring uncertainty quantification.  
