    \end{figure}
	\section{Conclusion}\label{section-5}
	In this draft, we have presented a novel temporal semi-discrete numerical scheme of the CHNS equations using the time filter technique and have analyzed the unconditional stability and convergence of the backward Euler time filter (BETF) scheme. By incorporating the time filter technique into the backward Euler (BE) framework, we have shown that the computational complexity remains almost unchanged while improving the time order of the BE scheme by one. Through three numerical examples, we have demonstrated the effectiveness of the time filtered scheme in enhancing both temporal accuracy and applying to some practical problems. Based on these results, we plan to extend to adaptive BETF algorithms and high-order algorithms characterized by conceptual simplicity and low computational cost.

