\subsubsection{Position Adjustment}
To align with the designated orientation $\beta$ determined through Fourier descriptors, the control for yaw is adjusted to match $\beta$. The position errors $\hat{\epsilon}_{p1}$ for the UAV are defined as:

\begin{equation}
\hat{\epsilon}_{p}:
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&\hat{e}_{px} = \hat{d} \cos (\beta - \hat{\psi}) \cos(\gamma) - d_{\beta} \\
&\hat{e}_{py} = \hat{d} \sin (\beta - \hat{\psi}) \sin(\gamma) \\
&\hat{e}_{pz} = (Z_c - d_{\beta} \sin (\gamma)) - Z
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation}

with

\begin{equation}
\lim_{t \to \infty} \hat{\epsilon}_{p}(t) = 0
\end{equation}

To satisfy this position control goal, the position control strategy applied is:

\begin{equation}
\begin{bmatrix}
\dot{\hat{e}}_{px} \\
\dot{\hat{e}}_{py} \\
\dot{\hat{e}}_{pz}
\end{bmatrix} =
\begin{bmatrix}
f \left(\sum_{j=1}^{3} kp_{xj} \epsilon p_{xj}, \bar{V}_{x}, \bar{D}_{x}, 0\right) \\
f \left(\sum_{j=1}^{3} kp_{yj} \epsilon p_{yj}, \bar{V}_{y}, \bar{D}_{y}, 0\right) \\
f \left(\sum_{j=1}^{3} kp_{zj} \epsilon p_{zj}, \bar{V}_{z}, \bar{D}_{z}, 0\right)
\end{bmatrix} = \vec{V}
\end{equation}

Note that the parameters $kp_{xj}, kp_{yj}, kp_{zj}$ are to be tailored. $\Vec{V} = (V_x, V_y, V_z)^T$ is the linear velocity vector of the UAV with $V_x, V_y$ and $V_z$ the maximal linear velocities reached when the position errors are above the distances $\bar{D}_{x}$, $\bar{D}_{y}$, and $\bar{D}_{z}$. For more details, readers are directed to \cite{Petitprez2023}. \\

