        1 > \alpha_1 \vee \beta_{-1} \geq \alpha_1 \wedge \beta_{-1} > \alpha_{-1} \vee \beta_{1} \geq \alpha_{-1} \wedge \beta_{1} > \alpha_{2} \vee \beta_{-2},
    \end{equation*}
    and the inequalities for $m\geq 2$ follow by an induction argument. It is readily seen that $1>\alpha_1,\beta_{-1}$. Now due to the construction and monotonicity of the functions $u^*$ and $v^*$ in \eqref{eq:def_ustar_vstar}, we have:
    \begin{align*}
        &\alpha_1 =u^*(\beta_0) > u^*(\beta_{-1}) = \alpha_{-1}\quad \text{and}\quad
