\begin{abstract}
    We show that for any class of Boolean algebras with an associative operator, if it contains the complex algebra of $(\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{N}), \cup)$, its equational theory is undecidable. Equivalently, any associative normal modal logic valid over the frame $(\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{N}), \cup)$ is undecidable. This settles a long-open question on the decidability of hyperboolean modal logic~\cite{GorankoVakarelov}, and addresses several related problems.
\end{abstract}



\section{Introduction}\label{introduction}

