\begin{highlights}
\item A comparison framework is provided to compare four frequency-constrained unit commitment methods with a base case unit commitment formulation, regarding the system benefits and computational burden perspectives.
\item Two performance indices are introduced to help analyze and compare the formulations more effectively by considering the under-frequency load shedding reduction.
\item Each formulation is implemented on a real Spanish island power system illustrating its effectiveness in real-world systems and helping operators choose the suitable method in different circumstances.
