To clearly distinguish the different models discussed in the previous subsections, each model is clearly defined with the corresponding constraints in \Cref{tab:models}. The maximum \gls{rocof} constraint presented in \cref{rocof} is added to the analytical \gls{cfcuc} formulation to achieve a more fair comparison. It is important to note that the non-linear constraints should be linearized before being added to the formulation, as discussed earlier.
