In Fig.~\ref{fig:3}e, we report the efficiencies of the gears as a function of the operating conditions $x$ and $y$ for $n =12$, keeping the same convention as before and with standard physiological conditions defined in Appendix~\ref{app:Standard physiological conditions} and summarized in Table~\ref{Tab:Standard physiological conditions}.
