	In this section, we review neutral-atom quantum computing and surface-code FTQC, highlight the current operational capabilities and state-of-the-art theories, and propose a scalable implementation that serves as the basis of our overall framework.
	In Sec.~\ref{sec:intro-atom}, we provide an overview of the neutral-atom array platform for implementing the FTQC, focusing on two prominent physical implementations employed: the zoned and the selective gate approach.
