On the other hand, the spin current is strongly enhanced for $K_1\ne K_2$.
In this case, the magnon dispersion has an energy gap at the $\Gamma$ point, and the band degeneracy is lifted there.
As a result, the FMR peaks are well separated compared with the case of $K_1=K_2$.
In Fig.~\ref{fig:K1not=K2}, we show the spin current induced by spin pumping as a function of the microwave frequency $\Omega$ for $K_1 = 0.004J$ and $K_2 = 0.005J$.
The other parameters are set as the same values in Fig.~\ref{fig:K1=K2}.
We find that the peak position depends only on the magnetic anisotropy $K_1$ and $K_2$ and is independent of $J_1$ and $J_2$. 
We also find that the spin current is largely enhanced from the case of $K_1=K_2$ and is even larger than that in the FI-NM junction.

